  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Individual Measure to Strengthen Border Management Capacities in Bosnia and Herzegovina</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2017, there has been a significant increase in the number of people transiting through Bosnia and Herzegovina (BiH), which has strained the country&apos;s migration and border management capacities. Technical capacities for borders management remain limited, given the logistical difficulties posed by the long border with Croatia, Serbia, and Montenegro and the inaccessibility of certain regions. There is a need for better document management mechanisms, border surveillance human and technical capacities to prevent cross-border crime, and inter-institutional cooperation on these issues, especially between the actors at the border and in the interior. This project aims to address the abovementioned challenges, while responding to the objectives of the EU Action Document - Individual measure to strengthen border management capacities in favour of the Western Balkans for 2022. The Overall Objective of this project, which is in line with the EU Action Plan and relevant BiH strategies, is to improve Integrated Border Management in line with the human rights of migrants in Bosnia and Herzegovina. IOM aims to contribute to the following Outcomes: Outcome 1: Improved capacities of BiH to effectively manage their borders Outcome 2: Strengthened capacities of BiH border management beneficiaries to implement migration policies in line with EU standards.</narrative>
  </description>
